Benefits/Characteristics
    - High Availability
        Services experience Very little down time
        Measured by a percentage (Uptime vs downtime)
        5 Nines - 99.999%
        Multiple servers holding up a website, so if one goes down, then the other one is available
    - Scaleabiity
        Able to increase the amount  of items in a system at a linear rate or less than a linear rate
        Vertical Scaling (Scale Up)
            - Including more resources like RAM, CPUs, Memory to handle a high amount of volume
        Horizontal Scaling (Scale Out)
            - Instead of one server holding all the volume, you distribute it across multiple.
    - Elasticity
        Ability to scale up or down quickly
        With a random burst of volume, you will need to be able to capture all of it quick by scaling automatically
    - Metered Utilization
        Pay-per-Use basis
            - # of users
            - # of connections
            - # of stored data
        Metered vs Measured
            Metered = Per-Use                       Ex.Water Bill (The more you use, the more you pay)
            Measured = Plan/Subscription            Ex.Netflix (Monthly subscription)
    - Shared resources
        Minimize the cost by putting VMs on other servers
        Splits resources amoungst users to only give what they need while saving the extra for someone else to use
    - File synchronization
        Ability to store data which can then spread to other places depending on configuration